{"object": "whatsapp_business_account", "entry": [{"id": "2303959047073307", "changes": [{"value": {"messaging_product": "whatsapp", "metadata": {"display_phone_number": "15556698871", "phone_number_id": "1332015746651819"}, "contacts": [{"profile": {"name": "Arokiya Gilbrit....\u2605"}, "wa_id": "918072851813", "user_id": "IN.1564551011177259"}], "messages": [{"from": "918072851813", "from_user_id": "IN.1564551011177259", "id": "wamid.HBgMOTE4MDcyODUxODEzFQIAEhgWM0VCMDY2NkVGMUY1OEIxQzE5MzgxNwA=", "timestamp": "1789134091", "text": {"body": "FIX PROMPT \u2014 RESTORE MOCK PAYMENT GATE + AUTOMATIC LANGUAGE DETECTION\n\nIMPORTANT:\nDO NOT TOUCH EXISTING FUNCTIONALITIES.\n\nThis is a targeted fix for TWO issues only:\n\n1. Mock payment is being bypassed before appointment confirmation.\n2. Bot is not consistently responding in the same language used by the patient.\n\nDO NOT rewrite working appointment, reschedule, cancellation, doctor availability, patient, reports, emergency, WhatsApp webhook, RAG, dashboard, authentication, or escalation functionality.\n\n========================================================\nPART A \u2014 FIX MOCK PAYMENT INTEGRATION\n========================================================\n\nCURRENT BUG:\n\nThe current flow is:\n\nAppointment details\n        \u2193\n[Confirm Appointment]\n        \u2193\nAppointment Confirmed\n\nThis is WRONG.\n\nThe mock payment step is missing/bypassed.\n\nThe patient must NEVER receive:\n\n\"Appointment confirmed!\"\n\nuntil the mock payment has successfully completed.\n\n========================================================\n1. REQUIRED BOOKING FLOW\n========================================================\n\nThe correct flow must be:\n\nDoctor Selection\n        \u2193\nDate Selection\n        \u2193\nReal Available Time Slots\n        \u2193\nClickable Time Slot\n        \u2193\nSlot Revalidation\n        \u2193\nAppointment Preview\n        \u2193\nPatient clicks \"Confirm Appointment\"\n        \u2193\nPAYMENT METHOD SELECTION\n        \u2193\nMOCK PAYMENT\n        \u2193\nPAYMENT SUCCESS\n        \u2193\nFINAL APPOINTMENT CONFIRMATION\n\nDo NOT change the existing steps before this point.\n\n========================================================\n2. CONFIRM APPOINTMENT MUST NOT BOOK DIRECTLY\n========================================================\n\nWhen the patient clicks:\n\n[Confirm Appointment]\n\nDO NOT immediately:\n\n- mark appointment as CONFIRMED\n- send appointment confirmation\n- send confirmation email\n- send success notification\n\nInstead:\n\n1. Validate appointment details.\n2. Revalidate selected slot.\n3. Retrieve the existing doctor consultation fee.\n4. Create/reuse a PENDING mock payment.\n5. Ask the patient to select a payment method.\n\n========================================================\n3. PAYMENT SCREEN\n========================================================\n\nAfter the patient clicks:\n\n[Confirm Appointment]\n\nshow:\n\n\"Please complete the consultation payment to confirm your appointment.\"\n\nDisplay:\n\nDoctor: Dr. James R\nDepartment: ENT\nDate: 12 September 2026\nTime: 10:00 AM\n\nConsultation Fee: \u20b9200\n\n\"Select your payment method:\"\n\nClickable options:\n\n[GPay]\n[PhonePe]\n[Paytm]\n[UPI]\n[NetBanking]\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nThe \u20b9200 shown above is ONLY an example.\n\nAlways retrieve the actual consultation fee from the existing doctor/fee data.\n\nDO NOT hardcode \u20b9200.\n\n========================================================\n4. MOCK PAYMENT ONLY\n========================================================\n\nDO NOT integrate:\n\n- Razorpay\n- Stripe\n- PayU\n- Cashfree\n- real UPI gateway\n- real GPay\n- real PhonePe\n- real Paytm\n- real bank gateway\n\nThis is a POC.\n\nUse the existing PostgreSQL mock payment implementation/table if already present.\n\nIf the payment table was already created, REUSE IT.\n\nDo NOT create duplicate payment tables.\n\n========================================================\n5. PAYMENT DATA\n========================================================\n\nUse the existing payment structure if already implemented.\n\nIf the implementation exists, preserve its fields.\n\nPayment should be associated with:\n\npatient_id\nappointment_id\namount\ncurrency\npayment_method\npayment_status\ntransaction_reference\ntimestamps\n\nPayment methods:\n\nGPAY\nPHONEPE\nPAYTM\nUPI\nNETBANKING\n\nStatuses:\n\nPENDING\nSUCCESS\nFAILED\nCANCELLED\n\nDo not modify existing database structures unnecessarily.\n\n========================================================\n6. MOCK PAY ACTION\n========================================================\n\nAfter patient selects:\n\n[GPay]\n\nshow:\n\n\"Mock payment\"\n\nAmount:\n\u20b9200\n\nPayment Method:\nGPay\n\nThen provide a clickable:\n\n[Pay \u20b9200]\n\nAgain:\n\nDO NOT hardcode \u20b9200.\n\nThe button must dynamically display:\n\n[Pay \u20b9{actual consultation fee}]\n\nExample:\n\n[Pay \u20b9500]\n\nif the selected doctor's consultation fee is \u20b9500.\n\n========================================================\n7. MOCK PAYMENT SUCCESS\n========================================================\n\nWhen patient clicks:\n\n[Pay \u20b9200]\n\nthe system should execute the existing mock payment flow.\n\nGenerate a unique mock transaction reference.\n\nExample:\n\nMOCK-TXN-XXXXXXXX\n\nSet payment:\n\nPENDING\n        \u2193\nSUCCESS\n\nDo not use a real payment provider.\n\n========================================================\n8. PAYMENT SUCCESS MUST GATE CONFIRMATION\n========================================================\n\nOnly after:\n\npayment_status = SUCCESS\n\nmay the appointment become confirmed.\n\nRequired sequence:\n\npayment SUCCESS\n        \u2193\nfinal slot revalidation\n        \u2193\nappointment transaction\n        \u2193\nappointment CONFIRMED\n        \u2193\nnotification\n        \u2193\nsuccess response\n\nIf payment fails:\n\npayment_status = FAILED\n\nDO NOT confirm appointment.\n\nIf payment is cancelled:\n\npayment_status = CANCELLED\n\nDO NOT confirm appointment.\n\n========================================================\n9. APPOINTMENT + PAYMENT MUST BE CONSISTENT\n========================================================\n\nDo not create a confirmed appointment without successful payment.\n\nThe final appointment confirmation must verify:\n\npatient_id exists\ndoctor_id exists\ndepartment_id exists\nappointment_date exists\nappointment_time exists\nselected_slot_id exists\nslot_revalidated = true\npayment_id exists\npayment_status = SUCCESS\n\nIf any required condition is missing:\n\nDO NOT confirm.\n\n========================================================\n10. IDEMPOTENCY\n========================================================\n\nPrevent duplicate payment and duplicate booking if:\n\n- patient clicks Pay twice\n- WhatsApp sends duplicate callback\n- webhook is retried\n- patient refreshes/repeats the action\n\nUse existing idempotency mechanisms where available.\n\nDo not create:\n\ntwo payments\ntwo appointments\ntwo confirmation messages\n\nfor one patient action.\n\n========================================================\n11. EXISTING APPOINTMENT CONFIRMATION MUST REMAIN\n========================================================\n\nAfter successful payment, preserve the existing confirmation message format.\n\nIt should include:\n\nAppointment confirmed!\n\nPatient:\nGil Christ\n\nPatient ID:\nexisting patient code\n\nDoctor:\nDr. James R\n\nDepartment:\nENT\n\nDate:\nexisting selected date\n\nTime:\nexisting selected time\n\nAppointment ID:\nexisting appointment ID\n\nPayment:\nPAID\n\nPayment Method:\nselected method\n\nTransaction Reference:\nmock transaction reference\n\nDo not remove existing confirmation details.\n\n========================================================\n12. DO NOT BYPASS PAYMENT THROUGH FREE TEXT\n========================================================\n\nIf patient says:\n\n\"Confirm\"\n\ninside appointment confirmation state,\n\nthis should trigger the existing confirmation action and then payment.\n\nIt must NOT directly confirm the appointment.\n\nIf patient says:\n\n\"Yes\"\n\nsame behavior.\n\nThe appointment must still pass through payment.\n\n========================================================\nPART B \u2014 AUTOMATIC LANGUAGE DETECTION\n========================================================\n\nSECOND ISSUE:\n\nThe patient should be able to communicate naturally in any currently supported language.\n\nThe bot MUST respond in the same language used by the patient.\n\n========================================================\n13. LANGUAGE DETECTION RULE\n========================================================\n\nUse the existing LLM-based language detection architecture.\n\nDo NOT introduce:\n\n- regex language detection\n- keyword matching\n- hardcoded language phrases\n- language-specific if/else rules\n\nThe LLM should semantically identify the language of the patient's latest meaningful message.\n\n========================================================\n14. SUPPORTED LANGUAGES\n========================================================\n\nPreserve all currently supported languages:\n\nENGLISH\nTAMIL\nHINDI\nTELUGU\nMALAYALAM\nKANNADA\nURDU\n\nDo not remove or rename existing language values.\n\n========================================================\n15. RESPONSE LANGUAGE\n========================================================\n\nRULE:\n\nPATIENT LANGUAGE \u2192 BOT RESPONSE LANGUAGE\n\nExamples:\n\nPatient:\n\"Hi\"\n\nBot:\nEnglish\n\nPatient:\n\"\u0bb5\u0ba3\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bae\u0bcd\"\n\nBot:\nTamil\n\nPatient:\n\"\u0b8e\u0ba9\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b92\u0bb0\u0bc1 appointment \u0bb5\u0bc7\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd\"\n\nBot:\nTamil\n\nPatient:\n\"\u092e\u0941\u091d\u0947 \u0905\u092a\u0949\u0907\u0902\u091f\u092e\u0947\u0902\u091f \u091a\u093e\u0939\u093f\u090f\"\n\nBot:\nHindi\n\nPatient:\n\"\u0c28\u0c3e\u0c15\u0c41 \u0c05\u0c2a\u0c3e\u0c2f\u0c3f\u0c02\u0c1f\u0c4d\u200c\u0c2e\u0c46\u0c02\u0c1f\u0c4d \u0c15\u0c3e\u0c35\u0c3e\u0c32\u0c3f\"\n\nBot:\nTelugu\n\nThe bot should respond naturally in the detected language.\n\n========================================================\n16. LANGUAGE MUST APPLY TO THE ENTIRE WORKFLOW\n========================================================\n\nLanguage detection must NOT work only for greetings.\n\nIt must apply to:\n\nGreeting\nAppointment booking\nDoctor selection\nDepartment selection\nDate selection\nTime selection\nPayment\nAppointment confirmation\nMy Appointments\nCancellation\nReschedule\nPatient Reports\nHospital Information\nEmergency\nHuman Handoff\nError messages\n\nExample:\n\nPatient is speaking Tamil.\n\nThen payment should be:\n\n\"\u0b89\u0b99\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd \u0b9a\u0ba8\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc8 \u0b89\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0b9f\u0bc1\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4 \u0b86\u0bb2\u0bcb\u0b9a\u0ba9\u0bc8 \u0b95\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0ba3\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bc8 \u0b9a\u0bc6\u0bb2\u0bc1\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bb5\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd.\"\n\nwith Tamil payment options.\n\nThe appointment confirmation should also be in Tamil.\n\n========================================================\n17. BUTTON LABELS MUST FOLLOW LANGUAGE\n========================================================\n\nIf the patient language is Tamil:\n\nuse Tamil labels where supported.\n\nExample:\n\n[Google Pay]\n[PhonePe]\n[Paytm]\n[UPI]\n[Net Banking]\n\nand appropriate Tamil explanatory text.\n\nIf English:\n\n[Google Pay]\n[PhonePe]\n[Paytm]\n[UPI]\n[NetBanking]\n\nDo not force the entire conversation back to English.\n\nBrand/payment names can remain unchanged where appropriate.\n\n========================================================\n18. LANGUAGE PERSISTENCE\n========================================================\n\nStore the detected language in the existing:\n\nconversation.language\n\nfield.\n\nOnce detected, maintain it throughout the active conversation.\n\nExample:\n\nPatient:\n\"\u0bb5\u0ba3\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bae\u0bcd\"\n\nconversation.language = TAMIL\n\nThen:\n\nPatient:\n\"\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0bb3\u0bc8\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bc1 appointment \u0bb5\u0bc7\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd\"\n\nBot responds in Tamil.\n\nPatient:\n\"10 AM\"\n\nBot should continue in Tamil because the short message is context-dependent and does not provide enough evidence for a language switch.\n\n========================================================\n19. LANGUAGE SWITCHING\n========================================================\n\nIf the patient explicitly changes language, detect it.\n\nExample:\n\nPatient:\n\"\u0bb5\u0ba3\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bae\u0bcd\"\n\nBot:\nTamil\n\nPatient:\n\"Show my appointments\"\n\nBot:\nEnglish\n\nThe workflow state must remain unchanged.\n\nOnly the response language changes.\n\nDO NOT restart the conversation.\n\nDO NOT reset:\n\npatient_id\ndoctor_id\ndepartment_id\nappointment_date\nappointment_time\nselected_slot_id\npayment state\nworkflow state\n\n========================================================\n20. SHORT MESSAGES\n========================================================\n\nImportant:\n\nMessages such as:\n\n\"yes\"\n\"no\"\n\"10 AM\"\n\"tomorrow\"\n\"same doctor\"\n\"change it\"\n\nmay not contain enough language information.\n\nDo NOT run an unreliable language switch from these short context-dependent messages.\n\nUse the existing conversation language unless the LLM has strong evidence that the patient intentionally switched language.\n\n========================================================\n21. LLM RESPONSE GENERATION\n========================================================\n\nThe response-generation layer must receive:\n\ncurrent conversation language\ncurrent workflow state\npatient's latest message\nrelevant structured context\n\nand generate the response in:\n\nconversation.language\n\nDo not allow an English fallback to overwrite an established Tamil/Hindi/etc. conversation unnecessarily.\n\n========================================================\n22. DO NOT USE RAG FOR LANGUAGE DETECTION\n========================================================\n\nDo not retrieve language from hospital knowledge/RAG.\n\nLanguage is a conversation/session property.\n\nUse the existing LLM language understanding layer.\n\n========================================================\n23. TYPING INDICATOR\n========================================================\n\nPreserve the existing WhatsApp typing/processing implementation.\n\nWhile the bot is processing:\n\nstart typing/processing indicator.\n\nAfter response:\n\nstop it.\n\nDo not add fake:\n\n\"Typing...\"\n\ntext.\n\nDo not introduce artificial delays.\n\nDo not change existing WhatsApp webhook behavior unnecessarily.\n\n========================================================\n24. ROOT-CAUSE INVESTIGATION\n========================================================\n\nBefore coding, inspect the current payment flow and determine why:\n\nConfirm Appointment\n        \u2193\nAppointment Confirmed\n\nis bypassing:\n\nPayment Method\n        \u2193\nMock Payment\n        \u2193\nPayment Success\n\nInspect:\n\n- appointment confirmation handler\n- confirmation callback\n- payment service\n- payment table/model\n- payment state\n- conversation state\n- WhatsApp interactive callback handler\n- appointment transaction\n- notification trigger\n\nFind the exact bypass point.\n\nFix the root cause.\n\nDo NOT rewrite the appointment service.\n\n========================================================\n25. LANGUAGE ROOT-CAUSE INVESTIGATION\n========================================================\n\nInspect:\n\n- language detection\n- conversation.language\n- LLM intent router\n- response generator\n- WhatsApp response formatter\n- interactive button/list translation\n- session state\n\nFind why the bot sometimes responds in a language different from the patient's language.\n\nFix the existing architecture rather than adding hardcoded language rules.\n\n========================================================\n26. REGRESSION TESTS \u2014 PAYMENT\n========================================================\n\nTEST 1:\n\nPatient selects appointment slot.\n\nExpected:\nAppointment preview.\n\nTEST 2:\n\nPatient clicks Confirm Appointment.\n\nExpected:\nPayment method selection.\n\nNOT appointment confirmation.\n\nTEST 3:\n\nPatient selects GPay.\n\nExpected:\nMock payment screen.\n\nTEST 4:\n\nPatient clicks Pay.\n\nExpected:\nMock payment SUCCESS.\n\nTEST 5:\n\nAfter payment success.\n\nExpected:\nAppointment becomes CONFIRMED.\n\nTEST 6:\n\nPayment fails.\n\nExpected:\nAppointment is NOT confirmed.\n\nTEST 7:\n\nPatient clicks Pay twice.\n\nExpected:\nNo duplicate payment/appointment.\n\nTEST 8:\n\nExisting cancellation.\n\nExpected:\nStill works.\n\nTEST 9:\n\nExisting reschedule.\n\nExpected:\nStill works.\n\n========================================================\n27. REGRESSION TESTS \u2014 LANGUAGE\n========================================================\n\nTEST 10:\n\nTamil greeting.\n\nExpected:\nTamil response.\n\nTEST 11:\n\nTamil appointment request.\n\nExpected:\nEntire booking flow remains Tamil.\n\nTEST 12:\n\nHindi greeting.\n\nExpected:\nHindi response.\n\nTEST 13:\n\nTelugu greeting.\n\nExpected:\nTelugu response.\n\nTEST 14:\n\nPatient switches Tamil \u2192 English.\n\nExpected:\nEnglish response without resetting workflow.\n\nTEST 15:\n\nPatient sends \"yes\" during Tamil flow.\n\nExpected:\nContinue Tamil.\n\nTEST 16:\n\nPatient sends \"10 AM\" during Tamil flow.\n\nExpected:\nContinue Tamil.\n\n========================================================\n28. FINAL ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA\n========================================================\n\nPAYMENT:\n\n\u2713 Confirm Appointment does NOT directly confirm.\n\u2713 Payment method screen appears first.\n\u2713 Consultation fee comes from selected doctor's actual fee.\n\u2713 GPay works.\n\u2713 PhonePe works.\n\u2713 Paytm works.\n\u2713 UPI works.\n\u2713 NetBanking works.\n\u2713 Mock payment only.\n\u2713 No real payment gateway.\n\u2713 Payment success is required before confirmation.\n\u2713 Failed payment does not confirm.\n\u2713 Cancelled payment does not confirm.\n\u2713 Duplicate clicks do not create duplicate transactions.\n\u2713 Appointment and payment remain correctly linked.\n\u2713 Existing confirmation/notification behavior remains intact.\n\nLANGUAGE:\n\n\u2713 Patient language is detected automatically.\n\u2713 Bot responds in the same language.\n\u2713 Existing supported languages remain supported.\n\u2713 Language persists during the workflow.\n\u2713 Short context-dependent messages do not accidentally change language.\n\u2713 Intent/workflow state is not reset by language changes.\n\u2713 Buttons/options follow the conversation language where applicable.\n\u2713 No regex language detection is introduced.\n\u2713 No keyword-based language detection is introduced.\n\u2713 Existing multilingual functionality is preserved.\n\n========================================================\nMOST IMPORTANT RULE\n========================================================\n\nDO NOT TOUCH EXISTING FUNCTIONALITIES.\n\nMake the smallest possible targeted changes.\n\nDO NOT:\n\n- rewrite appointment booking\n- rewrite slot availability\n- rewrite reschedule\n- rewrite cancellation\n- rewrite WhatsApp webhook\n- rewrite patient management\n- rewrite dashboards\n- remove reports\n- remove emergency\n- remove human escalation\n- remove RAG\n- remove voice functionality\n- replace the existing LLM architecture\n- introduce regex intent detection\n- introduce hardcoded language detection\n- integrate real payment gateways\n- hardcode consultation fees\n- hardcode payment success without executing the mock payment flow\n\nFix ONLY:\n\n1. Mock payment being bypassed before appointment confirmation.\n2. Automatic patient-language detection and same-language response.\n\nPreserve every existing working functionality.\n\nAfter implementation, run the full existing test suite and add regression tests for both issues.\n\nDO NOT TOUCH EXISTING FUNCTIONALITIES."}, "type": "text"}]}, "field": "messages"}]}]}
